  "caption": "Quinn hurt a shoulder moving house and planned to stay home until totally perfect. Weeks passed, the couch was winning, and worry about going back grew.\n\nStaying connected to work with modified, graded duties is often linked to better recovery than staying off completely until fully healed.\n\nWhat can help: modified duties with hours built up over a few weeks, a written plan with tasks, hours and review dates, having your physio look at your real job tasks and workstation, agreeing who to tell if it flares, and asking your doctor to describe what you can do, not just what to avoid.\n\nIf pain rises a lot, talk with your doctor and adjust the plan.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
